{%- comment -%}
  PDP — Country delivery date estimator.

  Renders a country picker plus a Standard and Express estimated delivery date.

  NOTE ON DATA SOURCE
  A theme cannot read Shopify shipping settings at runtime: Liquid has no access
  to delivery profiles, and the one storefront endpoint for live rates,
  /cart/shipping_rates.json, requires a non-empty cart a PDP visitor does not
  have. The rates table below is therefore baked, not live — generated from the
  Admin API (deliveryProfiles → locationGroupZones → methodDefinitions) and
  pasted into the `delivery_rates` setting. Regenerate it whenever the zones or
  prices change in Settings → Shipping and delivery.

  Transit days are NOT readable from the Admin API — DeliveryRateDefinition
  carries a price and no duration — so those columns mirror the transit times
  configured against each rate by hand.

  The picker lists localization.available_countries, i.e. exactly the countries
  the storefront actually sells to, so it can never drift from the markets. A
  country the rates table does not cover renders as unavailable rather than
  inventing a date for a lane that cannot be quoted.

  Accepts:
    delivery_rates   — one line per country: CODE|std_lo|std_hi|exp_lo|exp_hi|std_price|exp_price
                       "-" disables a tier. A ROW line, if present, catches
                       everything not named explicitly.
    standard_label / express_label — service names, e.g. Foreign Air
    cutoff_hour      — 0-23, read in delivery_timezone
    delivery_timezone — IANA zone the warehouse keeps, e.g. America/Los_Angeles
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign here = localization.country.iso_code | default: 'US' -%}

<div
  class="dest"
  data-delivery-estimator
  data-cutoff-hour="{{ cutoff_hour | default: 13 }}"
  data-timezone="{{ delivery_timezone | default: 'America/Los_Angeles' }}"
  data-country="{{ here }}"
>
  {%- comment -%}
    Parsed in JS rather than emitted as Liquid-built JSON: prices are free text
    ("Free over $150"), and hand-rolling JSON around arbitrary strings in Liquid
    is how quoting bugs get shipped. type="text/plain" is inert markup.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script type="text/plain" data-delivery-rates>{{ delivery_rates | default: 'US|3|5|1|2|$10|$20' | escape }}</script>

  {%- comment -%}
    Picker first, title under it. The country is the input the whole panel turns
    on, and it matches the Returns tab, which already leads with its picker.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="dest__entry">
    <label class="dest__hint" for="dest-country">Select your country</label>
    <div class="dest__row">
      <select id="dest-country" class="dest__select" data-dest-country>
        {%- if localization.available_countries.size > 0 -%}
          {%- for country in localization.available_countries -%}
            <option value="{{ country.iso_code }}" {% if country.iso_code == here %}selected{% endif %}>{{ country.name }}</option>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- comment -%} Markets not configured: at least quote where we stand. {%- endcomment -%}
          <option value="{{ here }}" selected>{{ localization.country.name | default: 'United States' }}</option>
        {%- endif -%}
      </select>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="dest__label">
    <span class="dest__pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    Delivery date estimator
  </p>

  {%- comment -%}
    Two rows, spec-table shape: service name and price on the left, the resolved
    dates on the right. The business-day counts are deliberately absent — the
    dates already say when it lands, and "3–5 business days" next to
    "Aug 6 – Aug 10" is the same fact twice in a weaker unit. The day counts
    still drive the arithmetic, they just aren't restated as copy.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="dest__results" data-dest-results hidden>
    <div class="dest__tier" data-dest-row="standard" hidden>
      <span class="dest__tier-label">{{ standard_label | default: 'Foreign Air' }}</span>
      <span class="dest__tier-price" data-dest-standard-price></span>
      <span class="dest__tier-date" data-dest-standard></span>
    </div>
    <div class="dest__tier" data-dest-row="express" hidden>
      <span class="dest__tier-label">{{ express_label | default: 'Express Air' }}</span>
      <span class="dest__tier-price" data-dest-express-price></span>
      <span class="dest__tier-date" data-dest-express></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Shown when the selected country has no line in the rates table. Saying so is
    the honest outcome — a country with no zone cannot be quoted here and cannot
    check out either, so inventing a date would only move the failure later.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <p class="dest__error" data-dest-error hidden>
    We don't ship here yet. <a href="{{ contact_url | default: '/pages/contact' }}">Ask us about it</a>.
  </p>
</div>
